{"term":"report","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:33ee4c6283da743fd0","definition":"To relate details of (an event or incident); to recount, describe (something).","example":"Many of these classic methods are still used, with some modern improvements. For example, with the aid of special microphones and automated sound detection software, ornithologists recently reported[…]that pine siskins (Spinus pinus) undergo an irregular, nomadic type of nocturnal migration.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive, transitive","wordFamily":["aforereported","coreport","mass report","misreport","outreport","overreport","reportability","reportable","reportative","report back","reportee","reporter","report for duty","reportorial","report out","rereport","underreport","unreported"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/report#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ab6b2155b594351012","definition":"To repeat (something one has heard), to retell; to pass on, convey (a message, information etc.).","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["aforereported","coreport","mass report","misreport","outreport","overreport","reportability","reportable","reportative","report back","reportee","reporter","report for duty","reportorial","report out","rereport","underreport","unreported"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/report#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7eb5bdb900ca775b75","definition":"To take oneself (to someone or something) for guidance or support; to appeal.","example":"thenne they ansuerd by and by that they coude not excuse the quene /[…]/ Allas sayd the quene I made this dyner for a good entente / and neuer for none euyl soo almyghty god me help in my ryght as I was neuer purposed to doo suche euylle dedes / and that I reporte me vnto god","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete, reflexive","register":"obsolete, reflexive","wordFamily":["aforereported","coreport","mass report","misreport","outreport","overreport","reportability","reportable","reportative","report back","reportee","reporter","report for duty","reportorial","report out","rereport","underreport","unreported"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/report#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:be9c2e41d68c215431","definition":"To notify someone of (particular intelligence, suspicions, illegality, misconduct etc.); to make notification to relevant authorities; to submit a formal report of.","example":"For insurance reasons, I had to report the theft to the local police station.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"formal","register":"formal, transitive","wordFamily":["aforereported","coreport","mass report","misreport","outreport","overreport","reportability","reportable","reportative","report back","reportee","reporter","report for duty","reportorial","report out","rereport","underreport","unreported"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/report#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:787882863bc64f6565","definition":"To make a formal statement, especially of complaint, about (someone).","example":"If you do that again I'll report you to the boss.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["aforereported","coreport","mass report","misreport","outreport","overreport","reportability","reportable","reportative","report back","reportee","reporter","report for duty","reportorial","report out","