reported","coreport","mass report","misreport","outreport","overreport","reportability","reportable","reportative","report back","reportee","reporter","report for duty","reportorial","report out","rereport","underreport","unreported"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/report#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:9ffb5e9cfe78de5f82","definition":"To return or present as the result of an examination or consideration of any matter officially referred.","example":"The committee reported the bill with amendments, or reported a new bill, or reported the results of an inquiry.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"dated","register":"dated","wordFamily":["aforereported","coreport","mass report","misreport","outreport","overreport","reportability","reportable","reportative","report back","reportee","reporter","report for duty","reportorial","report out","rereport","underreport","unreported"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/report#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d20583da8992dcd0b9","definition":"To take minutes of (a speech, the doings of a public body, etc.); to write down from the lips of a speaker.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["aforereported","coreport","mass report","misreport","outreport","overreport","reportability","reportable","reportative","report back","reportee","reporter","report for duty","reportorial","report out","rereport","underreport","unreported"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/report#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:94c5d5423bc6d928ae","definition":"To refer.","example":"Baldwine his ſonne, the fourth of that name [Baldwin IV of Jerusalem], ſucceeded his father [Amalric of Jerusalem]: ſo like unto him, that we report the reader to the character of King Almerick, and will ſpare the repeating his description.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["aforereported","coreport","mass report","misreport","outreport","overreport","reportability","reportable","reportative","report back","reportee","reporter","report for duty","reportorial","report out","rereport","underreport","unreported"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/report#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5e8227f4beafe70cd8","definition":"To return or repeat, as sound; to echo.","example":"a church with windows only from above[…] that reporteth the voice twelve or thirteen times","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"ambitransitive, obsolete, rare","register":"ambitransitive, obsolete, rare","wordFamily":["aforereported","coreport","mass report","misreport","outreport","overreport","reportability","reportable","reportative","report back","reportee","reporter","report for duty","reportorial","report out","rereport","underreport","unreported"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/report#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:cb2067c773bd2760f2","definition":"Of a ship, to return to a port.","example":"Our ship leaves port on Monday and will re-port on Friday.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["aforereported","coreport","mass report","misreport","outreport","overreport","reportability","reportable","reportative","report back","reportee","reporter","report for duty","reportorial","report out","rereport","underreport","unreported"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/report#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:37a30f296661fae594","definition":"A piece of information describing, or an account of certain events given or presented to someone, with the most common adpositions being by (referring to creator of the report) and on (referring to the subject).","example":"A report by the telecommunications ministry on the phone network revealed a severe capacity problem.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["aforereported","coreport","mass report","misreport","outreport","overreport","reportability","reportable","reportative","report back","reportee","reporter","report for duty","reportorial","report out","rereport","underreport","unreported"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/report#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:bd8a399d8bed596e50","definition":"Reputation.","example":"I love thee in such sort / As, thou being mine, mine is thy good report.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["aforereported","coreport","mass report","misreport","outreport","overreport","reportability","reportable","reportative","report back","reportee","reporter","report for duty","reportorial","report out","rereport","underreport","unreported"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/report#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:036c2a1e14d33a2481","definition":"The sharp, loud sound of a gunshot or explosion.","example":"While their masters, the mates, seemed afraid of the sound of the hinges of their own jaws, the harpooneers chewed their food with such a relish that there was a report to it.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["aforereported","coreport","mass report","misreport","outreport","overreport","reportability","reportable","reportative","report back","reportee","reporter","report for duty","reportorial","report out","rereport","underreport","unreported"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/report#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:19d7c26de947ec7fbd","definition":"An employee whose position in a corporate hierarchy is below that of a particular manager.","example":"The revelation that boss of one year Laurent Freixe was conducting an undisclosed affair with a direct report has rocked a 159-year-old conglomerate that pioneered infant formula and milk chocolate before growing to become the world's largest food and beverage company.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["subordinate"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["aforereported","coreport","mass report","misreport","outreport","overreport","reportability","reportable","reportative","report back","reportee","reporter","report for duty","reportorial","report out","rereport","underreport","unreported"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/report#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/ɹɪˈpɔːt/"},"wordFamily":["aforereported","coreport","mass report","misreport","outreport","overreport","reportability","reportable","reportative","report back","reportee","reporter","report for duty","reportorial","report out","rereport","underreport","unreported"]}